<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE HermitCrabInput SYSTEM "HermitCrabInput.dtd">
<!-- Morphotactic attribute breadth. Closes the coverage-ledger entries that need no phonological
     feature system: repetition caps, blocking, partial rules/entries, bound allomorphs, non-final
     templates, co-occurrence rules, and MPR feature groups. Stratum cyclicity and phonologicalRuleOrder
     are declared below (Main) purely for the enumerated value's presence in a document: grep the whole
     of src/SIL.Machine.Morphology.HermitCrab for "Cyclicity"/"PhonologicalRuleOrder" and Stratum.cs's
     own property list, and neither exists anywhere outside the DTD and XmlLanguageLoader's unread
     Stratum attribute text; the loader never even reads them into a discarded local, let alone acts
     on them. No fixture can make either surface observable; that is a product gap, not a modeling gap.

     Repetition is the reason this fixture exists at all. multipleApplication has NO effect on a rule
     reached through an AffixTemplate slot, because a template applies each slot once (established
     against the C# oracle in edge-cases/loader-isactive-breadth). Every repeatable rule here is
     therefore listed on the Stratum's own morphologicalRules attribute instead, where the cap is
     observable: mrRep0 must never apply, and mrRep2 must apply at most twice. Those two boundaries
     are what the ledger's remaining multipleApplication values are quotiented against.

     Main is linear rather than unordered deliberately: with several repeatable stratum-level rules an
     unordered stratum multiplies derivation orders and the word list stops being legible. That is also
     why MorphologicalRule@partial gets its OWN unordered Second stratum below: partial only gates a
     rule NOT reachable through any Slot (SynthesisAffixProcessRule.cs's IsTemplateRule check), and a
     template-then-stratum-rule ordering only exists via the Unordered ApplyTemplates-then-
     ApplyMorphologicalRules recursion in SynthesisStratumRule.cs, which Linear never takes.

     Every decoy carries isActive="no" and is named by the word whose outcome observes it, per
     words.yaml's neutralizes: lists. -->
<HermitCrabInput>
  <Language>
    <Name>MorphotacticAttributeBreadth</Name>
    <PartsOfSpeech>
      <PartOfSpeech id="posN"><Name>n</Name></PartOfSpeech>
    </PartsOfSpeech>
    <HeadFeatures>
      <SymbolicFeature id="featX"><Name>x</Name><Symbols><Symbol id="symVA">vA</Symbol></Symbols></SymbolicFeature>
    </HeadFeatures>
    <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatures>
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprA">A</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprB">B</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <!-- Bucket-2 coverage (MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures->MorphologicalInput.excludedMPRFeatures):
           an affix confers a flag that blocks a LATER affix - HCLoader.cs:969 (AffixProcessAllomorph.
           OutMprFeatures) writes the payload, HCLoader.cs:1717 (AffixProcessAllomorph.
           ExcludedMprFeatures) reads it. Ungrouped deliberately: this is a direct exclusion, not an
           overwrite-group interaction (see mrConferExcl/mrExclReader below). -->
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature id="mprExclFlag">ExclFlag</MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeature>
      <!-- outputType="append" adds to the stem's existing MPR features rather than replacing them;
           the default is overwrite. -->
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup matchType="all" outputType="append" features="mprA mprB">
        <Name>appendGroup</Name>
      </MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup>
      <!-- groupDecoy claims the SAME two features as appendGroup, so activating it hijacks mprA/mprB's
           group membership away from appendGroup instead of leaving it untouched (a decoy over a
           feature no rule sets would never compete with anything): the loader assigns each
           MprFeature's Group to whichever active group last claims it (MprFeatureGroup.cs's
           MprFeaturesChanged), so an isActive="no" decoy naming a DIFFERENT feature can never be a
           real control here. outputType is left at its default (overwrite) deliberately: that is the
           opposite of appendGroup's own "append", so activating this decoy also changes the group's
           effective output behavior, not just its identity. -->
      <MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup isActive="no" features="mprA mprB">
        <Name>groupDecoy</Name>
      </MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatureGroup>
    </MorphologicalPhonologicalRuleFeatures>
    <CharacterDefinitionTable id="tbl">
      <Name>Main</Name>
      <SegmentDefinitions>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sA"><Representations><Representation>a</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sE"><Representations><Representation>e</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sI"><Representations><Representation>i</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sO"><Representations><Representation>o</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sU"><Representations><Representation>u</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sB"><Representations><Representation>b</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sD"><Representations><Representation>d</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sG"><Representations><Representation>g</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sK"><Representations><Representation>k</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sL"><Representations><Representation>l</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sM"><Representations><Representation>m</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sN"><Representations><Representation>n</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sP"><Representations><Representation>p</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sR"><Representations><Representation>r</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sS"><Representations><Representation>s</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
        <SegmentDefinition id="sT"><Representations><Representation>t</Representation></Representations></SegmentDefinition>
      </SegmentDefinitions>
    </CharacterDefinitionTable>
    <NaturalClasses>
      <FeatureNaturalClass id="ncAny"><Name>Any</Name></FeatureNaturalClass>
    </NaturalClasses>
    <Families>
      <Family id="famBlk">Blk</Family>
      <Family id="famBlk3">Blk3</Family>
    </Families>
    <Strata>
      <!-- cyclicity="cyclic" and phonologicalRuleOrder="simultaneous" are both non-default. This
           stratum declares no phonological rules, so the rule-order value is a load-time property
           here rather than an observable ordering; the ledger records it accordingly. -->
      <Stratum characterDefinitionTable="tbl" morphologicalRuleOrder="linear" cyclicity="cyclic"
               phonologicalRuleOrder="simultaneous"
               morphologicalRules="mrRep0 mrRep2 mrConferExcl mrExclReader"
               isActive="yes">
        <Name>Main</Name>
        <MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
          <!-- multipleApplication="0": the cap is zero, so this suffix must never attach. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrRep0" multipleApplication="0" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>neverApplies</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subRep0">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stem0"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stem0" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ba</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NEVER</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>never</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- multipleApplication="2": at most two copies of this suffix. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrRep2" multipleApplication="2" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>twiceAtMost</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subRep2">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stem2"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stem2" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>de</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>TWICE</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>twice</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrNF" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>nfOnly</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subNF">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemNF"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemNF" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>pu</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>NF</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>nf</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- blockable="false": exempt from blocking by a more specific competing form. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrUnblockable" blockable="false" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>unblockable</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subUnblockable">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemU"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprA"><CopyFromInput index="stemU" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>gi</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <OutputHeadFeatures><FeatureValue feature="featX" symbolValues="symVA" /></OutputHeadFeatures>
            <MorphemeId>UNBLK</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>unblk</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- partial="true": a partially specified rule. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrPartial" partial="true" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>partialRule</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subPartial">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemP"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemP" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>mo</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>PART</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>part</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- blockable="false" on a realizational rule, plus an inactive realizational decoy. -->
          <RealizationalRule id="mrReal" blockable="false">
            <Name>realUnblockable</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subReal">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemR"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemR" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ru</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>REAL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>real</Gloss>
          </RealizationalRule>
          <RealizationalRule id="mrRealDecoy" isActive="no">
            <Name>realDecoy</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subRealDecoy">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemRD"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemRD" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>si</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>RDEC</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>rdec</Gloss>
          </RealizationalRule>
          <!-- mrCoA/mrCoB/mrCoC exist solely so AllomorphCoOccurrenceRule/MorphemeCoOccurrenceRule
               adjacency values have a fixed, three-morpheme ordering to be checked against, isolated
               from every other construct in this fixture so a co-occurrence delta never also depends
               on UNBLK/PART/REAL's own MPR/blocking machinery. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>sa</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>coa</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ka</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>cob</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoC" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coC</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoC">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoC"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoC" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ta</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COC</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>coc</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrCoD" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>coD</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subCoD">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemCoD"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemCoD" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>na</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>COD</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>cod</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- mrMB/mrMA/mrMReq exist solely to make appendGroup's outputType (and groupDecoy's
               isActive) observable: mrMB sets mprB, mrMA sets mprA (both members of appendGroup), and
               mrMReq then requires mprB still be present. Under append (baseline), setting mprA does
               not evict mprB, so mrMReq succeeds; under overwrite (the outputType mutation, or
               groupDecoy hijacking both features into its own overwrite-by-default group), setting
               mprA evicts mprB and mrMReq fails. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrMB" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>setMB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subMB">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemMB"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprB"><CopyFromInput index="stemMB" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>bu</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>MB</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>mb</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrMA" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>setMA</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subMA">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemMA"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprA"><CopyFromInput index="stemMA" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>bi</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>MA</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>ma</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrMReq" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>reqMB</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subMReq">
                <MorphologicalInput requiredMPRFeatures="mprB"><PhoneticSequence id="stemMReq"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemMReq" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>du</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>MREQ</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>mreq</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- Bucket-2 coverage: the affix-conferred-blocking pair. mrConferExcl's own
               MorphologicalOutput.MPRFeatures write (mprExclFlag) is the writer under test; applying
               it before mrExclReader means mrExclReader's own MorphologicalInput.excludedMPRFeatures
               gate blocks - a later affix refusing to attach once an earlier one has marked the stem,
               e.g. a derivational suffix that makes a further derivation ineligible. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrConferExcl" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>conferExcl</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subConferExcl">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemConferExcl"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput MPRFeatures="mprExclFlag"><CopyFromInput index="stemConferExcl" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>do</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>CONFEREXCL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>conferexcl</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrExclReader" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>exclReader</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subExclReader">
                <MorphologicalInput excludedMPRFeatures="mprExclFlag"><PhoneticSequence id="stemExclReader"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemExclReader" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>ri</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>EXCLREADER</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>exclreader</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
        </MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
        <AffixTemplates>
          <!-- The FINAL template. A stratum whose only template is non-final admits no complete word
               at all (confirmed against the C# oracle: with just the non-final template below, even a
               bare root produced zero parses), so a final template has to exist alongside it. -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>finalTemplate</Name>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrUnblockable"><Name>unblockableSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrPartial"><Name>partialSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrReal"><Name>realSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrRealDecoy"><Name>realDecoySlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrCoA"><Name>coASlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrCoB"><Name>coBSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrCoC"><Name>coCSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrCoD"><Name>coDSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrMB"><Name>mbSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrMA"><Name>maSlot</Name></Slot>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrMReq"><Name>mreqSlot</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
          <!-- final="false": a non-final template. Its output is not a complete word on its own. -->
          <AffixTemplate requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" final="false">
            <Name>nonFinalTemplate</Name>
            <Slot optional="true" morphologicalRules="mrNF"><Name>nonFinalSlot</Name></Slot>
          </AffixTemplate>
        </AffixTemplates>
        <LexicalEntries>
          <LexicalEntry id="eKul" partOfSpeech="posN" ruleFeatures="mprA">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aKul"><PhoneticShape>kul</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
              <!-- isBound="true": this allomorph cannot stand as a free word. -->
              <Allomorph id="aKulBound" isBound="true"><PhoneticShape>kur</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>KUL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>vessel</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <!-- partial="true": a partially specified entry. -->
          <LexicalEntry id="eNap" partOfSpeech="posN" partial="true">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aNap"><PhoneticShape>nap</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>NAP</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>stone</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eSol" partOfSpeech="posN">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aSol"><PhoneticShape>sol</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>SOL</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>rope</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eBak" partOfSpeech="posN" family="famBlk">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aBak"><PhoneticShape>bak</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>VAK</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>bak</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eDom" partOfSpeech="posN" family="famBlk">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aDom"><PhoneticShape>dom</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <AssignedHeadFeatures><FeatureValue feature="featX" symbolValues="symVA" /></AssignedHeadFeatures>
            <MorphemeId>ZOM</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>dom</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eSim" partOfSpeech="posN" family="famBlk3">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aSim"><PhoneticShape>sim</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <AssignedHeadFeatures><FeatureValue feature="featX" symbolValues="symVA" /></AssignedHeadFeatures>
            <MorphemeId>SIM</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>sim</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eRog" partOfSpeech="posN" family="famBlk3">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aRog"><PhoneticShape>rog</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <AssignedHeadFeatures><FeatureValue feature="featX" symbolValues="symVA" /></AssignedHeadFeatures>
            <MorphemeId>ROG</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>rog</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
          <LexicalEntry id="eTop" partOfSpeech="posN">
            <Allomorphs>
              <Allomorph id="aTop"><PhoneticShape>top</PhoneticShape></Allomorph>
            </Allomorphs>
            <MorphemeId>TOP</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>top</Gloss>
          </LexicalEntry>
        </LexicalEntries>
      </Stratum>
      <!-- Second, unordered stratum: MorphologicalRule/partial="true" needs a stratum-level (never
           templated) rule to be attempted AFTER a final template already applied, and that ordering
           only arises via the Unordered ApplyTemplates->ApplyMorphologicalRules recursion
           (SynthesisStratumRule.cs); Main is deliberately Linear (see its own header comment), so
           this construct gets its own stratum rather than disturbing that. -->
      <Stratum characterDefinitionTable="tbl" morphologicalRuleOrder="unordered" morphologicalRules="mrPO">
        <Name>Second</Name>
        <MorphologicalRuleDefinitions>
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrPogAffix" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>pogAffix</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subPogAffix">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemPogAffix"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
                <MorphologicalOutput><CopyFromInput index="stemPogAffix" /><InsertSegments><PhoneticShape>li</PhoneticShape></InsertSegments></MorphologicalOutput>
              </MorphologicalSubrule>
            </MorphologicalSubrules>
            <MorphemeId>POGAFX</MorphemeId>
            <Gloss>pogafx</Gloss>
          </MorphologicalRule>
          <!-- partial="true": never a member of any Slot, so it stays IsTemplateRule=false and this
               is the rule the mutation actually exercises. -->
          <MorphologicalRule id="mrPO" partial="true" requiredPartsOfSpeech="posN" outputPartOfSpeech="posN">
            <Name>afterFinal</Name>
            <MorphologicalSubrules>
              <MorphologicalSubrule id="subPO">
                <MorphologicalInput><PhoneticSequence id="stemPO"><OptionalSegmentSequence min="1" max="-1"><SimpleContext naturalClass="ncAny" /></OptionalSegmentSequence></PhoneticSequence></MorphologicalInput>
